  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "If the p-th powers in a finite p-group form a subgroup, must that subgroup\nbe powerful? That is, for p ̸= 2, if the p-th powers in a p-group of exponent p2 form a\nsubgroup, must that subgroup be abelian? For a 2-group of exponent 8, if the squares\nform a subgroup, must that subgroup be abelian?                               L. Wilson",
